121: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
122:     """
123:     Reflect the solid rectangular source objects across the full separator line and color the gap with the separator color.
124: 
125:     Input structure:
126:     - A dominant background contains one full-width or full-height one-pixel
127:       separator line in a non-background color.
128:     - One other foreground color forms solid rectangular objects, all strictly on the same side of that separator.
129:     - Remaining non-background pixels are scattered distractors.
130: 
131:     Rule:
132:     - Keep the input grid shape and unchanged pixels outside each affected corridor.
133:     - Mirror each source object across the separator line.
134:     - For every source object, recolor the rectangular strip between the
135:       original object and its reflection to the separator color, then paint the
136:       reflected object in the source color.
137: 
138:     Key insight:
